(`Set roster to [...]` at top level is one of the three spellings of a write
 to an already-declared name (LANGUAGE.md, "Type Immutability"), so the
 function reading the global must still see the global. The write used to be
 read as a rival declaration of an untyped name, which took `roster` out of
 the definite-declaration map altogether and left the reader with nothing to
 read - docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #92.)

a list called roster is [].

To 'how many'.
    Return a number, roster's length.

Set roster to ["ada", "grace"].
Print 'how many'.
